26,2,,status,Mizuki,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
27,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
28,2,,status,Victoria,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
29,2,,status,George,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"My findings suggest a pattern: projects that benefit a single wing are poorly rated, while shared, bookable spaces are highly valued.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Victoria,,"That aligns with my data. General-purpose rooms are in desperate demand, while specialist rooms sit idle for most of the term.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,George,,"I've found that our grounds and front-of-house staff are severely depleted, yet some technicians still have capacity in their schedules.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The schedules are worrying. Comfort-based projects often slip by a year, and outdoor work is frequently delayed by weeks of bad weather.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"It seems the market is shifting. Mechanical and ducting costs have risen significantly, and we have no reserves for replacing old AV kit.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Victoria, if general rooms are the bottleneck, we should prioritize a project that increases that capacity rather than adding more specialist suites.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"I agree, @Toshio. Furthermore, we must consider that any room taken out of service requires expensive off-site hiring to maintain the timetable.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,George,,"@Benjamin, if mechanical costs are rising, we should be cautious about complex ventilation projects that might blow the budget.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that is a good point. Also, any plan involving extensive outdoor work risks those weather-related delays I discovered.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed. We are facing a trifecta of rising costs, staffing shortages in specific areas, and a history of schedule slippage.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"I also found that older blocks often hide hazardous materials, which can add months of delay before a contractor even starts.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"@Toshio, that makes the risk of renovating older ground-floor spaces quite high. We need a plan with minimal structural surprises.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,George,,I noticed that bench technicians are wasting hours on manual tasks that modern equipment should handle automatically.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, that suggests a technical upgrade could actually relieve some of the staffing pressure you are concerned about.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"A fascinating intersection of needs. We need something that is cost-stable, low-risk in timing, and high-utility for the general population.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
