55,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Looking at the candidates, the Central Study Commons seems most aligned with the high ratings for bookable, shared spaces.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Victoria,,I agree. The Commons addresses the shortage of general-purpose rooms and avoids the high-cost specialist room trap.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,George,,"The Laboratory Ventilation Upgrade would solve the technicians' manual routine issues, but @Benjamin mentioned the rising cost of ducting.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"The Path Network is too risky given the weather delays. The Media Center might slip if it's seen as a ""comfort"" project.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"The Commons is a conversion of an existing hall, which should be more cost-predictable than a full mechanical overhaul of labs.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@George, while the labs help technicians, the Commons serves the entire campus, which the post-occupancy data suggests is the key to success.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Mizuki, the Commons is indoors, avoiding the rain and frost delays that plague the Path Network.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mizuki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,George,,"I see the logic. If the Commons uses a service desk, we must ensure it doesn't further strain the unfilled front-of-house posts.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"@George, a simple service desk is manageable. The Commons is the most likely to stay on schedule compared to the others.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,It avoids the hazardous material risks of deep structural work in older blocks and the volatility of mechanical tenders.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I am convinced. The Central Study Commons maximizes utility and minimizes the risk of disappointment.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Victoria,,I concur. It solves the booking crisis for general rooms with the least disruption to the timetable.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,George,,"If it is the most stable choice for the budget and schedule, I can support it, provided the staffing is handled.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Mizuki,,It is the most realistic plan. I vote for the Central Study Commons.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,The logic is inescapable. It is the most elegant solution to our systemic constraints. I vote for the Central Study Commons.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for the Central Study Commons.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Victoria,,I vote for the Central Study Commons.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,George,,I vote for the Central Study Commons.,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
